                <divLine xml:id="m-f9aadec6-228b-454a-8f77-b825d8a04354" facs="#m-07194fc1-ba12-45e9-89e6-53e8a43df7b4" form="maxima" />
              </layer>
            </staff>
            <div xml:id="m-425151da-5726-4351-94d1-b7b6fb2a7a0f">
              <lg xml:id="m-bd44b65f-4136-4aa5-bb2e-585f89180d3b">
                <l xml:id="m-c95b8534-e440-43db-a1f9-6f5bcaaffaca" facs="#m-31271b7b-6388-4861-9e40-f52ef342c5b0" label="ambiguous">784</l><l xml:id="m-a0491ff7-cde7-4dd2-ae62-69c94b4c8481" facs="#m-0b78b592-ce61-4282-9bc1-94b687f75446" label="text-like">omce and Mass on Easter day</l><l xml:id="m-e74c43ba-8758-4904-83f1-1186837b6b2d" facs="#m-3d802a9b-7438-4a79-a98d-02c40a6c2f28" label="lyrics-like">The X. Benedicámus Dómino is sung in this manner at Vespers and at</l><l xml:id="m-bfc9d151-545d-4c72-944d-451a9f6ad517" facs="#m-b13fe0f5-917a-48a1-9795-95b64e5504d1" label="text-like">Lauds from this day till Saturday before Low Sunday. On Easter Sunday.</l><l xml:id="m-7f7101d4-adce-45c0-a989-102391ce40a0" facs="#m-16cb01bb-3c08-4c8e-89c8-7547d6e6d7ef" label="text-like">however, and on the tuo folloming days, the Y. may be sung as follows:</l><l xml:id="m-940aadef-e3b9-4370-afcb-c5155704b3ad" facs="#m-98e1b2fb-5896-437c-a150-571144b3da90" label="lyrics-like">V. Benedicámus Dó¬ mi- no, alle-lú-ia, alle¬ lú¬ ia</l><l xml:id="m-ff4ff9cf-0c47-4f5a-bed4-40623232c6cf" facs="#m-43153ff1-2d0b-43e4-8e58-36bc1dc720ba" label="lyrics-like">N. Dé¬ grá¬</l><l xml:id="m-10de0165-1f9f-4146-9ae1-5a29d1dce9d9" facs="#m-ad7cdf6e-c92a-471c-b279-313620351d20" label="lyrics-like">ti- as, alle- lú-ia, alle¬ lú- ia.</l><l xml:id="m-8549ae1c-3257-4d46-b364-9c9eff4c9252" facs="#m-ecfe64e4-31e8-460d-bb32-1b5ef83a9802" label="text-like">AT COMPLINE.</l><l xml:id="m-2d1b0193-a090-4a26-9748-5f64c579ebb6" facs="#m-e043d6b1-f0b1-4e91-ac98-dda2f6a9c36c" label="lyrics-like">Júbe, dómne. — Short Lesson. Fratres: Sóbrii estóte. — Y. Adiutórium</l><l xml:id="m-12d1f361-33af-4021-92f1-556d1482fc31" facs="#m-b408dcac-9e36-4493-8193-7c3a7d8046c1" label="lyrics-like">nóstrum. Pater noster. Confiteor. Misereátur. Indulgéntiam. Y. Convérte nos.</l><l xml:id="m-3e0eb2d6-7f06-4ba0-aece-c1eb5f7db322" facs="#m-0f37bff0-3200-48a8-bf9b-382c4087c19b" label="lyrics-like">V. Déus in adjutórium. Glória Pátri. Alleltia. The Fsalms of Sunday are sung</l><l xml:id="m-b9fc62d0-91e0-495b-8a97-af1a94bcc231" facs="#m-e8ad3391-ce00-44cf-b9b6-835e4d345876" label="text-like">in the tone S. G. p. 264. The following Antiphon is then sung:</l><l xml:id="m-3ce5f928-1dc3-4ca0-9337-0894a8e48d06" facs="#m-f7e23bb6-c18d-4168-a075-8cd0fbca9249" label="ambiguous">Ant.</l><l xml:id="m-5c6e8b4a-fcf7-4b6b-8cfa-1ef40635efeb" facs="#m-f68880b7-b07e-480b-8c73-715a36ff605e" label="ambiguous">8.</l><l xml:id="m-2cbb087e-fa2a-472e-a958-a5c3fa4aac66" facs="#m-c6449e36-9322-486a-b79f-8bb856d027d5" label="lyrics-like">Lle-lú-ia, alle-lú-ia,</l><l xml:id="m-1558419e-ba6f-4c50-bc4e-8f9073638840" facs="#m-c2f48e11-f287-40fa-9f44-83e0af99ef38" label="lyrics-like">alle-lú-ia, alle-lú-ia.</l><l xml:id="m-cc5db54e-62a3-4395-96e7-a0f090ef85e0" facs="#m-c775be87-778b-4ead-869c-f1c554b4a1e0" label="text-like">The Canticle Nunc dimittis. is next sung:</l><l xml:id="m-b0a50a1a-e60b-4cb2-80b6-4cf8147b0d1d" facs="#m-97df48c7-d4fe-481b-8aca-02d85038a3da" label="text-like">Canticle of Simeon.</l><l xml:id="m-0e330367-c362-4532-bbe7-e2e14d4068c6" facs="#m-c57f66ee-ae70-43c1-af6e-067d1be068f0" label="lyrics-like">1. Nunc dimittis sérvum tú-um Dómine, “ secúndum vérbum</l><l xml:id="m-0fe220fa-0915-4607-8073-5e11b2409454" facs="#m-cc6f023c-5d2c-48a7-ad9f-8422a5253083" label="lyrics-like">tú-um in pá¬ ce. 2. Qui-a vidé-runt.. 3. Quod parásti“ etc.</l><l xml:id="m-43219dbc-f52f-43ac-b310-17584704c7d8" facs="#m-86995a76-2b9f-4d31-8a15-c2681bd5e79e" label="lyrics-like">2. Quia vidérunt ócuti méi *salutáre túum.</l><l xml:id="m-3abb8626-b270-4039-9c2b-33309a1af50f" facs="#m-89676c87-6e14-4a1a-8cba-81efa57f73aa" label="lyrics-like">3. Quod parásti “ ante fáciem ómnium populórum:</l><l xml:id="m-3a8bb9e2-4dae-4588-83c9-3b4121153b38" facs="#m-72600dd2-41ca-43c4-a7d1-4d0266dd345a" label="lyrics-like">4. Lúmen ad revelatiónem géntium, * et glóriam plébis túde Israel.</l><l xml:id="m-1a18e2d6-7162-4dcb-8312-57eda0134f77" facs="#m-6f76bcaa-431e-4bf5-8bc7-b7d98bc3e520" label="lyrics-like">5. Glória Pátri, et Filio, * et Spirítui Sáncto.</l><l xml:id="m-83221693-24cd-49f8-a1be-6469c35aa8ad" facs="#m-ae277ed0-d7f5-4a88-852e-c6172abee4c1" label="lyrics-like">6. Sicut érat in princípio, et nunc, et sémper, * et in saécula saecutó¬</l><l xml:id="m-4396e53f-03ba-4fb5-9d51-3e5b66b9d864" facs="#m-7d95a2b2-d3a2-4c27-a41a-6ad7f00a1621" label="ambiguous">rum. Amen.</l><l xml:id="m-f1080f13-5423-4a23-b527-f46b4c3d2dfe" facs="#m-4fcc8317-595f-47e2-8b98-09d4c56221c0" label="lyrics-like">The Ant. Haec dies. p. 783. is next said; then the Prayer Visita, quaésumus.</l><l xml:id="m-d73004cd-8b4b-4076-95d6-201f01cea54e" facs="#m-bc7ef9e5-2178-4605-8f29-f9b9b4f8bd9a" label="text-like">with all that follows, p. 278.</l><l xml:id="m-866c55a5-071d-45c4-bc01-feab75d40d10" facs="#m-253e5fdd-239a-4726-a4b5-9bf676b59dd1" label="text-like">During the Octave of Easter until Vespers on the Saturday exclusive,</l><l xml:id="m-dc183f03-42d0-4b7c-a52e-ceed380b996b" facs="#m-e4288684-a608-49b0-85ad-6b1d30547f09" label="text-like">the Ofice of Easter Sunday is said at each ot the Hours, excent the prayer</l><l xml:id="m-61ff3924-bb1e-46b4-8abb-861640cd1366" facs="#m-96befa9d-6801-41eb-9fd5-ec85ddfc816d" label="text-like">and the Antiphon of the Magnificat. which are proper for each day. On</l><l xml:id="m-6365a80f-1d6d-4805-a354-1437032014e3" facs="#m-f76feeb9-4554-4ced-9491-e2146694cef6" label="text-like">Monday and Tuesday, the Ofice is ot double rite; on the other days, ot</l><l xml:id="m-0300ddf1-b586-4660-843a-7b4ed17cfb30" facs="#m-af10b68e-478b-419d-a547-6d82acf285c8" label="lyrics-like">semi-dõuble.</l></lg>
            </div>
          </section>
        </score>
      </mdiv>
    </body>
  </music>
</mei>